#              Herobrine's Scythe
# ==================================================
item.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.name=Herobrine's Scythe

research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.name=Herobrine's Scythe
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.text=Tear the flesh. Feed the war.

research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.0=You forged the Sickle of Abundance to bow the wheat and gather the harvest. It was a farmer's blessing, an echo of nature's gift. You remember stroking its edge beneath the moon, listening to its quiet hum—a song about harvest.<BR>But you grew greedy. You no longer wished to understand the life and death of crops. You wished to understand life itself.
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.1=You placed it upon the Infusion Altar, inked with death-knowledge, sealed with void-essence, carving runes that should never have been carved. The moment the altar's violet light died, the wheat-song fell silent—replaced by heartbeats. Thousands upon thousands of tiny heartbeats, trembling along its edge.<BR>It no longer craved the harvest. It craved a different kind of reaping.
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.2=It began to remember every strike. As the kill-count climbed through 30, 120, 450, 1500, it awakened through five stages: First Sight, First Stirring, Bloodthirst, Frenzy, Pale Eye. With each awakening, the edge blushed redder; the aura burned brighter.<BR>When the count reaches 99,999, it will complete its transformation into a cursed artifact—attack surging to 999. And you will not be able to turn back.
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.3=The first hand to hold it has its soul bound to the blade. A UUID is carved deep into the steel. Should another try to take it, the blood-light will cast them out—and whisper a warning into your ear.<BR>It knows you. It knows only you.<BR>If you ever wish to pass it on, you must first erase your own mark. No one has ever spoken of what that takes.
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.4=Every torn body releases a small pulse of energy, leaping between nearby foes—from one to the next, until nothing remains standing. The pulse strikes with the full weight of the scythe itself.<BR>One swing. A line of blood-light. This is how it reaps its harvest.
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.5=Hold right-click, and it becomes a crimson barrier. The damage reduction grows with each tier; in its final form, it will completely negate all harm.<BR>Meanwhile, it drains Vis from every living thing within eight blocks—beast and player alike—gathering the essence into threads of blood-red light that fuel your wands and amulets. It does not kill. It only takes.<BR>But divinity is never free. Each draught leaves a scratch upon its edge. Only by feeding it—your satchel, your wand, your own durability—will it choose to stay.
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.6=It hungers for blood. The deeper your wounds, the more it gives back—feeding you, and feeding itself.<BR>The price: your soul is stained with warp. Higher tiers, deeper stains. One day you will see those whitened eyes in your own reflection.
research.magianaturalis.herobrines_scythe.page.7=When you finally reap the 99,999th soul, it falls silent. No longer humming. No longer hungering.<BR>You hold it, and feel a peace you have never known—and an emptiness that reaches into your bones. Your eyes changed color that day. You did not look into a mirror. But you knew.<BR>You are no longer a thaumaturge. You are its master. You are its vessel. You are its next meal.

