research.magianaturalis.revealing_goggles.name=Bauble of Goggles
research.magianaturalis.revealing_goggles.text=Truth, Worn Around the Neck What Azanor Never Did

research.magianaturalis.revealing_goggles.page.1=You've grown tired of strapping the Goggles of Revealing to your skull every single day. It hogs your helmet slot, leaving no room for the gear that actually matters.<BR>More times than you care to admit, you've found yourself wondering: that old man in the Void — when, exactly, will he finally make these into a bauble?<BR><BR>To hell with Azanor. He won't.

research.magianaturalis.revealing_goggles.page.2=So you took matters into your own hands.<BR><BR>Through the rites of Magia Naturalis, you shrank the goggles down and reshaped them, until they fit snugly in your amulet slot. Your helmet slot is finally your own again.<BR>No more agonizing over that single stubborn inch above your head.

research.magianaturalis.revealing_goggles.page.3=Now you can wear your Goggles of Peering alongside any headpiece you like — a Silverwood Crown, a pair of Arcane Goggles, or one of those legendary helmets you never quite dared to use.<BR><BR>It carries every function of the advanced Goggles of Revealing, and grants near-limitless Night Vision on top. Take it off, and the blessing fades.<BR><BR>Sure, you *could* wear this and a regular pair of Goggles of Revealing at the same time. They won't fight each other — nodes and aspects will still show up just fine. You'll simply have one pair of lenses too many strapped to your face.<BR>If you're really going to do that, then pray tell: what exactly did you research this thing for?

