# ==================================================
# Mask Theory
# ==================================================
research.magianaturalis.mask_theory.name=Mask Theory
research.magianaturalis.mask_theory.text=Attitude is the Mask of the Heart

research.magianaturalis.mask_theory.page.1=Azanor once sought to condense "Attitude" itself into a mask. He placed it upon his face, yet it would not stay, no matter how he bound it with magic.<BR><BR>The mask laughed silently: "I see. You have no heart. Attitude is the mask of the heart. How can you wear me if you have no heart?"<BR><BR>Azanor understood—he had given his heart to the pursuit of knowledge. One without a heart cannot wear the mask of attitude.<BR><BR>In other words, for one who has a heart, attitude is itself a mask.

research.magianaturalis.mask_theory.page.2=§c§l"Beneath the mask—is there a heart, or none?"<BR><BR><IMG>magianaturalis:textures/misc/eldritchajor2.png:0:0:255:255:0.5</IMG>

research.magianaturalis.mask_theory.page.3=Azanor stared at the mask in his hands—the one that would not stay—and fell silent for a long while.<BR><BR>He understood at last. Attitude is never conjured from nothing. It grows from the heart. Where the heart holds something, attitude takes shape; where the heart holds nothing, attitude is but an empty shell, scattered by the faintest breath of wind.<BR><BR>And so it is in the world.<BR><BR>Before your elders, you wear deference. Before an enemy, you wear coldness. Before a true friend, you take off every mask and let the heart show. This is not hypocrisy—quite the contrary. It is the proof of having a heart. Because the heart knows who stands before it, the face reveals the fitting attitude.<BR><BR>Those who show the same face to all are not necessarily at peace. It may simply be that there is nothing within them at all.

research.magianaturalis.mask_theory.page.4=One without a heart cannot wear attitude. For attitude is not worn—it is revealed.<BR><BR>Every mask in your hands is the embodiment of an attitude within. To wear it is not to hide yourself, but to let the heart show itself to the world in the most direct way.<BR><BR>Beneath the mask—is the heart.

# ==================================================
# Grinning Devil Mask
# ==================================================
research.magianaturalis.mask_grinning_devil.name=Grinning Devil Mask
research.magianaturalis.mask_grinning_devil.text=A Grin Against the Grind
research.magianaturalis.mask_grinning_devil.page.1=Wearing this mask grants you a curious ability to blunt the effects of warp. It cannot prevent warp from occurring, but it can diminish the severity of its erosion.<BR><BR>It seems that grinning in the face of life's hardships does yield its own rewards.<BR><BR>——<BR><BR>You did not make it an attachment to the Thaumium Fortress Helm. You shrank it, reshaped it, and turned it into an independent mask that can be worn in the amulet slot.<BR>From now on, you need not sacrifice an entire headpiece for the sake of a single mask. It is still a mask—only in a different form.

# ==================================================
# Angry Ghost Mask
# ==================================================
research.magianaturalis.mask_angry_ghost.name=Angry Ghost Mask
research.magianaturalis.mask_angry_ghost.text=Asking For It
research.magianaturalis.mask_angry_ghost.page.1=On the battlefield, any creature that strikes you while you wear this grim mask has a chance to suffer the withering decay.<BR><BR>Truly asking for it.<BR><BR>——<BR><BR>You did not fix it to a helmet. You made it into a mask that hangs at your chest, a bauble.<BR>Fury need not sit upon the head—it has always lived in the heart.

# ==================================================
# Sipping Fiend Mask
# ==================================================
research.magianaturalis.mask_sipping_fiend.name=Sipping Fiend Mask
research.magianaturalis.mask_sipping_fiend.text=Should You Worry?
research.magianaturalis.mask_sipping_fiend.page.1=While wearing this mask, your attacks sometimes siphon the lifeblood of other creatures to strengthen yourself.<BR><BR>The act of draining them does not, in truth, feel as strange as you might expect.<BR><BR>But you wonder—should you be worried about that?<BR><BR>——<BR><BR>You made this mask into a bauble as well. Resting against the neck, where it always belonged.<BR>The pulse at your throat speaks closer to the truth than any expression on your face.

