research.magianaturalis.mask_attitude.name=Attitude Mask
research.magianaturalis.mask_attitude.text=Attitude is the mask of the heart

research.magianaturalis.mask_attitude.page.1=The last page of Azano's notes depicted a mask that would not stay on his face.<BR><BR>He finally understood — an attitude is not something conjured from nothing. It grows from the heart. Where the heart holds something, attitude takes shape; where the heart is empty, attitude is but a hollow shell.<BR><BR>Having already crafted three masks — Grinning, Angry, Sipping — what if all three were melted together, along with the heart each represents, into a single truly wearable mask?<BR><BR>He dipped the three masks into the primal spring, using his heart as a guide and his soul as fuel.<BR><BR>Three days and nights later, a new mask surfaced — carrying no attitude at all, yet carrying all attitudes at once.<BR><BR>He named it simply: Attitude.

research.magianaturalis.mask_attitude.page.2=[No Attitude]§r The Observer.<BR>§rNot contending, not raging, not acting.<BR><BR>Hostile creatures no longer single you out.<BR>Strike first, and the attitude falters.<BR>Should someone insist, their blow may miss — and recoil.

research.magianaturalis.mask_attitude.page.3=[Friendly]§r Blend with the light.<BR>§rLower yourself, and the world no longer guards against you.<BR><BR>Neutrals do not flee; hostility fades faster.<BR>Pursuers forget within three steps.<BR>Even when struck, attackers soften and withdraw.

research.magianaturalis.mask_attitude.page.4=[Solemn]§r Still as a mountain.<BR>§rYou do not fight — yet the enemy yields first.<BR><BR>The aura halts all living things within eight paces.<BR>No attack, no pursuit.<BR>You yourself are strengthened.

research.magianaturalis.mask_attitude.page.5=[Hiding]§r Flowers in the mist.<BR>§rYou are still there — others simply cannot see you clearly.<BR><BR>Your form fades; monsters' gaze slides past.<BR>Cost: primal vis from your wand.<BR>When vis runs dry, the mist disperses.

